PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Disagreement persists on C vs E (now split ~even). Confirmed variable chars from matrix (glabrous 1+4, simple eye 1+2+4, serrate 1+4, claws 2+4, ant absent 5 only; ancestral = setose/no-simple/no-serrate/no-claws/present-ant). 

C optimization (5 outgroup + ((4,1),2) clade): ant loss=1, glab+serrate=2 on (1+4), simple-eye gain=1 on ((1,4),2), claws=2 independent → total 6 steps. E: simple-eye gain+loss=2 (or equiv.), total 7. Other trees ≥8–11 (extra homoplasy on texture/serrate or antennae regain). 

Matrix + explicit Fitch counts (Colleagues 3/1/9/10/4) confirm C shortest; E supporters note it recovers (1+4) and (2+3) pairs but overlook that C incurs no extra texture/serrate cost. No color or invariant traits affect ranking. No unresolved issues; C remains favored.}

